      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/02/us-coast-guard-says-it-has-intercepted-ship-carrying-fuel-to-cuba",
      "description": "<p>US says ship thought to be using common ‘dark fleet’ tactics was boarded and taken to Mexico as embargo continues</p><p>The US Coast ⁠Guard has announced that it intercepted a large cargo ship carrying fuel bound for <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/cuba\">Cuba</a>, as the ⁠Trump administration’s crippling ⁠oil embargo against ​the island nation continued.</p><p>The vessel named Grace was stopped on 5 September in the Caribbean Sea between Cuba ⁠and Mexico while using tactics to evade authorities, the Coast Guard said. The New York Times reported that the ship ⁠was 91 metres (300ft) long.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/02/us-coast-guard-says-it-has-intercepted-ship-carrying-fuel-to-cuba\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
